    pr_ref:  # fc6e
    description: "Found by the 11-06 adversarial review of the safety_zones wrappers (lab: wrapper_review_11062026/REVIEW.md #8, probe b/p8/).\n\nDefect: user_state_write(private=True) makes the FILE 0600 before writing (the #2072 fix holds), but creates its parent directories with the default mode (0755 under umask 022). Record names are sha256(resolved repo path)[:16].\n\nTrigger: a local user who can traverse the victim's home into ~/.local/state/hypergumbo.\n\nConsequence: that user can list the directory and confirm whether a guessed repo path has a recorded trust-backend / trust-catalogues / offer decision (not whether it was a grant or a decline). This partly defeats the privacy rationale in the docstring. Low: most homes are not traversable by others.\n\nFix direction: create the private record's directories 0700 (and tighten an existing one the wrapper created), with a test that pins the directory mode as well as the file mode."  # fc6e
    fields: {}  # fc6e
